comments.body:
@elarlang Thanks for the credits! I want to add that my colleague Pedram Hosseyni was and is involved in this work as well.

I fully agree that overlap with V52.2.3 should be avoided to ensure readers do not mix up the two requirements: Audience injection attacks can _only_ be prevented by the issuer of a token (by selecting an appropriate audience value). The receiver of a token cannot prevent these attacks, no matter what checks they apply to the audience value in the received token.

In any case, we are happy to provide examples/explanations as needed and to review proposed requirements - the one suggested by Elar above already went back and forth with us once.
